  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef considers the climate `HOT` if the temperature is **above** 202020, otherwise he considers it `COLD`. You are given the temperature CCC, find whether the climate is `HOT` or `COLD`.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains a single integer, the temperature CCC.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print on a new line whether the climate is `HOT` or `COLD`.\n\n\nYou may print each character of the string in either uppercase or lowercase (for example, the strings `hOt`, `hot`, `Hot`, and `HOT` will all be treated as identical).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤501 \\leq T \\leq 501≤T≤50",
      "0≤C≤400 \\leq C \\leq 400≤C≤40"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n21\n16",
        "output": "HOT\nCOLD",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The temperature is 212121, which is more than 202020. So, Chef considers the climate HOT.\nTest case 222: The temperature is 161616, which is not more than 202020. So, Chef considers the climate COLD."
      }
    ]
  },
